{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1541954-lasombra-antediluvian","id":1541954,"title":"Lasombra Antediluvian","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-09-11T22:42:32-07:00","id":1541954,"title":"Lasombra Antediluvian","content":"I posit the Lasombra Ante is not an &quot;Entity&quot; in &quot;The Abyss,&quot; but is living his best life in the body of Gratiano.<br /> <br /> According to the metafiction, &quot;L&quot; was unremarkable. A nobody. An experiment to see what would happen.<br /> <br /> But, Gratiano was of nobility, handsome, charismatic, generational wealth. A stereotypical &quot;Trust Fund Baby.&quot;<br /> <br /> I think &quot;L&quot; allowed himself to be diablerized, and then took over Gratiano's body.<br /> <br /> Think about it. A literal nobody with insane ambition for authority and power, weary of hiding from would-be dialblerists and his siblings, has the opportunity to possess the body of a literal prince. <br /> <br /> Yes, he took a small reduction in power, but he gained the respect, adulation, wealth, and social status he never had in mortal life, And he still has the power and knowledge to crush 99% of anyone who challenges him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\ude18","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25666-illuminostro","name":"Illuminostro","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-12T13:36:40-07:00","id":1541983,"title":"","content":"The lore doesn't support that theory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-12T15:39:48-07:00","id":1542003,"title":"","content":"It doesn't really fit the lore. The Founder is a creature that has ploughed the depths of the deep abyss and plundered all the lands of the Mediterranean, making entire empires crumble into dust. He is an immense divine creature whom all the Methuselahs of his clan absolutely feared. He was one of the architects of the fortunes of Rome and the expansion of the Arabs. He was the lord of one of the greatest vampiric realm of the middle age and Methuselah from an<br /> <br /> I doubt that a small time failed nobleman from a minor family in a suburban Italian shit-hotel had anything to offer someone like Lasombra, who by the way had already embraced people like Boukephos who was a real king.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-12T16:01:08-07:00","id":1542005,"title":"","content":"Hard to fathom that Gratino had anything else to offer his sire other then a potential tool/puppet and when compared to his &quot;siblings&quot; or 5th generation figures. He comes up very short and he could've suffered the same fate as the others did before Montano. Even folks like De Ruiz and his childe Moncada are more respected then this childe of Lasombra who comes across as a experiment.<br /> <br /> If anything he would see Montano as a more useful host as he was well respected and feared by the other members of the clan and kindred society in general.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 09-13-2024, 01:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-12T16:47:17-07:00","id":1542006,"title":"","content":"Much like their Tzimisce counterpart, the Lasombra founder almost certainly faked their destruction during the uprisings. At that level, they can easily Dominate any witnesses into believing anything they want, and are probably already existing as a being of pure shadow that only takes material form when it might be convenient (or just amusing) to do so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-12T18:40:36-07:00","id":1542009,"title":"","content":"I always viewed Gratino as a meat puppet that Lasombra uses to further his own schemes or distract others of the clan from reaching a state similar to his as I don't see him as someone who likes to share in his exhalted state.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-12T23:24:58-07:00","id":1542030,"title":"","content":"Why would Lasombra care about having a human title at this point. It\u2019s been the power behind countless thrones by this point, many we\u2019ve no longer even got records of. The whole Clan ethos is that titles don\u2019t matter, <i>power</i> matters. <br /> <br /> Lasombra giving up their current status of Clan founder just so they can chill in the body of someone who just happened to be born by the right parents makes no sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27967-caerolion","name":"Caerolion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-13T00:29:23-07:00","id":1542032,"title":"","content":"That is quite true that the 3rd generation days as living breathing humans were so long ago that such things as the original poster notion wouldn't even occur to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-13T10:46:55-07:00","id":1542068,"title":"","content":"It really is similar to the bit from Star Trek V. What does a several-thousand-year-old blood god need with any of the trappings of mortal wealth or prestige?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-13T10:54:10-07:00","id":1542069,"title":"","content":"Don't presume human mores or desires to beings who haven't been human longer then recorded history and seen everything and everyone that they knew and loved turned to dust and some of them are on a quest to move past a single physical form.<br /> <br /> 1.We have Gangrel becoming part of the Earth<br /> 2. Malkav seems to have become the Madness/Cobweb network<br /> 3. Tzmisce seems to have become Visscuitde itself and can manifest it self in any of it's line.<br /> 4. Lasombra is part of the void and I think uses Gratino as a puppet to interact with our world<br /> 5. Ventrue is perhaps now the Dominate Discipline<br /> 6. Set is in Duat and seemingly just watching his lineage .<br /> <br /> These don't seem like the actions of human beings anymore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-13T14:29:35-07:00","id":1542073,"title":"","content":"It depends on how you see the Antediluvians.<br /> <br /> Because the OP's post is describing the Mithras of Beckett's Jyhad Diary.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-13T16:00:46-07:00","id":1542077,"title":"","content":"I'm going with the idea that the 3rd generation don't think in such terms anymore and are significantly older then there direct childer and or grand childer that such trappings echoes of a more simple time and they are not the same beings anymore by any stretch of the imagination.<br /> <br /> Of course in our game the 3rd generation don't have much of active presence or if they truly involve themselves in the nightly activities of kindred so far down the line in terms of age of potency of the blood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 09-14-2024, 12:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-14T05:17:00-07:00","id":1542103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1541954-lasombra-antediluvian?p=1542073#post1542073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It depends on how you see the Antediluvians.<br /> <br /> Because the OP's post is describing the Mithras of Beckett's Jyhad Diary.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Not exactly. Beckett\u2019s Jyhad Diary gave us a Mithras that saw the increasing lengths of torpor and the growing Thirst as he aged, and sought to be diablerized as a way to circumvent the costs of aging.<br /> <br /> OP\u2019s post gives us a Lasombra that let himself be diablerized because \u201cbut I want a noble title written on my human birth certificate <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> \u201c<br /> <br /> How does Gratiano have more \u201crespect, adulation, wealth, and social status\u201d than the Antediluvian of his Clan?<br /> Again, why would Lasombra care about a mere title given by kine, when the entire philosophy of the Lasombra Clan is that power doesn\u2019t come from titles, it comes from influence? That sort of thinking is for clumsy Ventrue.<br /> <br /> My issue isn\u2019t the idea of an ancient vampire allowing his Diablerie to further his schemes, my issue is the thought of Lasombra giving even the slightest fraction of a shit about the title his physical body held during his mortal days, and being so wracked with impostor syndrome that he had to allow his Diablerie at the hands of a human prince so that he can have that sweet, sweet mortal title. <br /> <br /> Lasombra is, what, 10,000 years old? He has orchestrated the rise and fall of empires from the shadows. His title is Antediluvian of the Clan of Night. You think he\u2019s looking at the 14th Duke of Snobbington, and going \u201coh how I wish I had what HE had! That Dukedom is TRUE power. There\u2019s no other option. I must Embrace a mortal of noble birth and take over his body. Only that way will my new birth certificate call me Duke. That will show the other Antediluvians and teach them to laugh at me, who will soon be a Duke! With the power of that Dukedom behind me I shall be unstoppable!\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27967-caerolion","user":"Caerolion","date":". 09-14-2024, 08:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27967-caerolion","name":"Caerolion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-14T05:19:39-07:00","id":1542105,"title":"","content":"My own spin on the lore is lasombra is basically dead and thing floating around the abyss is the product of his failed apotheosis, the whole thing a 4d chess plan gone wrong.<br /> <br /> It's more compelling a setting if the damn things can actually die.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-14T05:25:02-07:00","id":1542107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caerolion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1541954-lasombra-antediluvian?p=1542103#post1542103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not exactly. Beckett\u2019s Jyhad Diary gave us a Mithras that saw the increasing lengths of torpor and the growing Thirst as he aged, and sought to be diablerized as a way to circumvent the costs of aging.<br /> <br /> OP\u2019s post gives us a Lasombra that let himself be diablerized because \u201cbut I want a noble title written on my human birth certificate <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> \u201c<br /> <br /> How does Gratiano have more \u201crespect, adulation, wealth, and social status\u201d than the Antediluvian of his Clan?<br /> Again, why would Lasombra care about a mere title given by kine, when the entire philosophy of the Lasombra Clan is that power doesn\u2019t come from titles, it comes from influence? That sort of thinking is for clumsy Ventrue.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, I don't have the same issue.<br /> <br /> The Lasombra Antediluvian wanting to live in the body of a lesser clan member to experience life differently doesn't strike me as so weird.<br /> <br /> One of the odder but interesting choices of THE OLD REPUBLIC was Vitiate grew bored being a God Emperor so he created his Children so he could experience life from different perspectives.<br /> <br /> He was still an Evil OverlordTM but it was his hobby.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-14T10:18:05-07:00","id":1542118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1541954-lasombra-antediluvian?p=1542107#post1542107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, I don't have the same issue.<br /> <br /> The Lasombra Antediluvian wanting to live in the body of a lesser clan member to experience life differently doesn't strike me as so weird.<br /> <br /> One of the odder but interesting choices of THE OLD REPUBLIC was Vitiate grew bored being a God Emperor so he created his Children so he could experience life from different perspectives.<br /> <br /> He was still an Evil OverlordTM but it was his hobby.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, to be honest. The idea that someone wouldn't want to live the good life because they have &quot;an alien mindset&quot; doesn't hold to me. Maybe cause I'm heavily Neurodivergent and have an alien mindset myself, so to speak.<br /> <br /> But aside agreeing with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar26986_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26986\" data-vbnamecard=\"26986\">Ragged Robin</a>, for me he's one who ultimately failed and died, the big problem with OP's proposal is the idea that Lasombra would need Gratiano, or the whole power redux thing, to have it.<br /> <br /> Of course, just as Mithras did, he could want the reduction for <b>other</b> reasons. But just to have a new identity? Even at worse case scenarios all he would need would be a few levels of Obfuscate or Vicissitude. Don't even dare to say an Antediluvian wouldn't have access to a few dots in an OoC.<br /> <br /> To be honest, my current default state for Arikel is precisely that she's living as a normal person, pretending to be mortal and enjoying life, but she has zero need to lose her powers to do so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":5826,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","user":"monteparnas","date":". 09-24-2024, 06:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-14T12:30:54-07:00","id":1542125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1541954-lasombra-antediluvian?p=1542118#post1542118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> To be honest, my current default state for Arikel is precisely that she's living as a normal person, pretending to be mortal and enjoying life, but she has zero need to lose her powers to do so.</div> </div> </div> </div>that's a neat idea, my concept for Arikel is she committed suicide a long time ago rather than lose her sense of humanity I have an easter egg antediluvian who never embraced with a similar outlook in my games however. She just pretends to be a caitiff with limited interest with vampire society, her actual passion is human development.<br /> <br /> I tend to avoid all the 3rd gen just a super nasty elder and tend to give them complex aghendas on a larger scale were they might not even interact with their clans, for example Gangrel is more interested in the restoration of pangea than anything wereas Set is way more concerned with Egyptian mythology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 09-14-2024, 03:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-14T12:48:34-07:00","id":1542127,"title":"","content":"To also the OP's credit, &quot;The Antediluvians faked their death by letting it seem like they got diablerized&quot; is the canon story.<br /> <br /> They just didn't want to get hassled anymore by their ungrateful childer and had been some of the most public Antes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-14T16:27:40-07:00","id":1542143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1541954-lasombra-antediluvian?p=1542107#post1542107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Lasombra Antediluvian wanting to live in the body of a lesser clan member to experience life differently doesn't strike me as so weird.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's certainly possible. However, the Antediluvians possess such a mastery of their Disciplines that these abilities effectively become plot devices. They could theoretically employ Dominate, Auspex, or a mix of both so as to inhabit a lesser clan member's body as if it were a mere costume, experiencing an alternate form of undeath at their whim without the need for diablerie.<br /> <br /> (The realization that such a thing can occur would likely be an unimaginable terror for anyone who became aware of it.)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-14T19:04:42-07:00","id":1542156,"title":"","content":"If an Antediluvian wants to experience life differently, it either possesses another person of their choice via Dominate, or takes on a false identity. I don\u2019t see how they would think the only way to do so would be to be Diablerized. But, the point remains that OP\u2019s post wasn\u2019t \u201cLasombra wanted different views\u201d, it was \u201cLasombra wanted the power that can only come from mortal titles\u201d. <br /> <br /> Lasombra HAS the good life. Its haven is literally a castle. Its supernatural influence is so great that it can take control not only of its own pawns but also influence the pawns of its own pawns. It has puppeteered countless rulers of every conceivable title, pulled the strings of those who believed they were the ones pulling the strings of those in power, and almost certainly also BEEN the one sitting on countless thrones too. <br /> <br /> Lasombra takes over Gratiano because it wants a younger body? Sure. Lasombra takes over Gratiano as a ploy to further the Jyhad? Absolutely. <br /> Lasombra taking over Gratiano because \u201cin the countless years I have roamed this world, the one thing I have always wanted and never been able to obtain was a noble status of my own\u201d? Hell no.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27967-caerolion","name":"Caerolion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-14T19:17:30-07:00","id":1542157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caerolion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1541954-lasombra-antediluvian?p=1542156#post1542156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If an Antediluvian wants to experience life differently, it either possesses another person of their choice via Dominate, or takes on a false identity. I don\u2019t see how they would think the only way to do so would be to be Diablerized. But, the point remains that OP\u2019s post wasn\u2019t \u201cLasombra wanted different views\u201d, it was \u201cLasombra wanted the power that can only come from mortal titles\u201d.<br /> <br /> Lasombra HAS the good life. Its haven is literally a castle. Its supernatural influence is so great that it can take control not only of its own pawns but also influence the pawns of its own pawns. It has puppeteered countless rulers of every conceivable title, pulled the strings of those who believed they were the ones pulling the strings of those in power, and almost certainly also BEEN the one sitting on countless thrones too.<br /> <br /> Lasombra takes over Gratiano because it wants a younger body? Sure. Lasombra takes over Gratiano as a ploy to further the Jyhad? Absolutely.<br /> Lasombra taking over Gratiano because \u201cin the countless years I have roamed this world, the one thing I have always wanted and never been able to obtain was a noble status of my own\u201d? Hell no.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, the real question is whether the Antediluvians know that diablerie does nothing to them or not.<br /> <br /> If it doesn't, then switching bodies with it isn't a problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-14T19:33:11-07:00","id":1542160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1541954-lasombra-antediluvian?p=1542105#post1542105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's more compelling a setting if the damn things can actually die.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that I prefer a setting where some antediluvians are actually destroyed. It makes the Jyhad real, and it lends itself to some cool distinctions between clans. A good mix of founders actually destroyed, believed destroyed but actually not, and survivors can make for some interesting scenarios and legends about Gehenna.<br /> <br /> <br /> However, in terms of Lasombra himself, I am of the mind that he has survived. He was never diablerized. IMO, the entire thing about Gratiano is that he was the ultimate test. We know from Children of the Inquisition that Lasombra had destroyed all his other childer by the time he embraced Montano because he always doubted their loyalty. So it doesn't make much sense that he embraced Gratiano in the way he did. He embraced Gratiano precisely because he was someone who already betrayed his own side. And almost immediately upon embrace, Gratiano began plotting to usurp his sire and take his place. Do we really believe that the Lasombra antediluvian as described in the Montano chapter is the same guy who couldn't see past Gratiano's sycophancy? His constant testing of the real limits of Lasombra's commands? Who couldn't believe Montano's own warnings? Unless he went senile during torpor, I cannot believe that.<br /> <br /> To me, the most likely scenario is that Lasombra used Gratiano to determine the true loyalties of his entire clan, most of whom were descended from the 4th generation childer he had already destroyed for failing to achieve his standards before embracing Montano. CotI says Lasombra &quot;craved faithfulness even beyond his final annihilation&quot; which means he wanted childer to be loyal to him even after his destruction. (That's an odd quote on its own unless we're supposed to realize it's a clue.) So what better test of his clan than to present them with his own destruction? Who remains loyal when that happens? Who turns out to be false?<br /> <br /> In-character descriptions in WoD sourcebooks always need to be taken with a grain of salt, examined critically, and compared to others. The chapters on Gratiano and Montano describe very different antediluvians. They are not the same character. I am pretty sure this was done on purpose to provide clues to the readers. We get Gratiano's chapter first in order to impress in our minds that Lasombra was just some fool who couldn't see the obvious in front of him. We're then given lots of information to the contrary in Montano's chapter, and I believe some critical clues that reveal the &quot;real story&quot;. But we ignore their implications because we're already used to the Gratiano version of events.<br /> <br /> I could be completely wrong as to the actual intent of the authors of CotI, but this is what I use for my chronicles as ST. Lasombra is very much around. Maybe he's in the Abyss or not, but he definitely has a physical body, and the Sabbat Lasombra are going to have a very big surprise for them when Gehenna happens. (One of the secret ironies in the WoD is that the Sabbat is wrong about almost everything. They didn't kill the two antediluvians they thought they did. Vestgeir almost certainly was not Caine. And much of their leadership and effective packs are members of the True Black Hand.) Later sourcebooks written by different authors under different developers had other ideas, and that's fine too if you want to use them.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude18","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-14T19:46:33-07:00","id":1542161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1541954-lasombra-antediluvian?p=1542105#post1542105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My own spin on the lore is lasombra is basically dead and thing floating around the abyss is the product of his failed apotheosis, the whole thing a 4d chess plan gone wrong.<br /> <br /> It's more compelling a setting if the damn things can actually die.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's essentially what happened with Cappadocius.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-15T08:12:53-07:00","id":1542174,"title":"","content":"I like the notion that Lasombra tried to become part of the Aybss and failed and all that is left nearly mindless fragments floating around and maybe some of them has some intelligence left but is very impotent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-15T21:42:57-07:00","id":1542219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1541954-lasombra-antediluvian?p=1542160#post1542160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, in terms of Lasombra himself, I am of the mind that he has survived. He was never diablerized.</div> </div> </div> </div>For now, at least, no one here said that Lasombra got Diablerized. I thoroughly agree that the Embracing of Gratiano was probably a ploy to reveal who was loyal.<br /> <br /> But the idea is that Lasombra died trying to become one with the Abyss. That's one thing I think improves the setting: that their plots for transcendence aren't infalible.<br /> <br /> The Antediluvians are, as far as stories go, each on a personal quest to achieve a higher state of existence. Well, why should those plots be safe, or guaranteed? Certainly, all those quests did have an impact in history, and possibly left some kind of vestige in the world. Some may even have succeeded.<br /> <br /> My point, though, is that not everything goes according to plan, and so some Antes failed, with mixed results, which may still mean something happened and even that consequences of their attempts linger in the world.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, though, my Lasombra died meeting the Abyss and Gratiano just found a dead corpse or not even that. The usurper accomplished their plan for no merit of their own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-15T22:03:36-07:00","id":1542220,"title":"","content":"I am of the opinion that Gratino at best destroyed an empty shell and he much like Montano had their memories adjusted by Lasombra so he could understand his new condition in peace. But that's my take and the one with him failing in that attempt and all is left is weak nearly mindless fragments.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-15T23:07:00-07:00","id":1542223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1541954-lasombra-antediluvian?p=1542161#post1542161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's essentially what happened with Cappadocius.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, i shuffled it around a bit where cappadocius' 'plan' is just the ravings of a madman and were never anything more than a pipe dream. By contrast lasombras plan made sense but just didnt work.<br /> It along with tzmisce and tremere leads into my plot point that you cannot transcend the curse with disciplines. Thats just a metaphysical trap. The closest is malkav and thats not what he was aiming for anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 09-16-2024, 02:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-15T23:07:16-07:00","id":1542224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1541954-lasombra-antediluvian?p=1542219#post1542219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For now, at least, no one here said that Lasombra got Diablerized.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless I misunderstood the original poster, that's pretty much how this thread was started. Even if others did not agree with it.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-15T23:11:49-07:00","id":1542225,"title":"","content":"for me Lucius or whatever the Antes name is this week, for sure died<br /> but for me, someone that was more Abyss than matter, can't be killed like that, it would had to be killed by the sun<br /> <br /> I think Gratiano drank his blood, and 'saw things' that left him somewhat devastated, a depth and deepness he couldn't fathom, making with a way bigger idea and fear of the world than he had... which made him more introspect than he ever was. So Gratiano is a tad shocked till this day in my view. <br /> <br /> Whatever the Clan of Shadows (sometimes I can't bring myself to call it by The-Shadow in Spanish, it's just too silly) Founder was, and whatever it became... well, for me is more liquid than solid at this point. He was dead already, he was just freed from physical and blood form. He was Shadow and Curse than Blood and bone. And who can say what is the soul of a Magister? It's already twisted... you mix it for thousands of years with the Void, and what you get? So I think Gratiano killed the dude, but he killed a mostly emptied husk. Lucius probably just wanted to become nothingness as it were, become as wide, as anonymous, and as undaunted as the Sea itself. Till he reached that state, he seemed like a very petty, self-doubting, self-hating old man, that couldn't even handle an honorous childer that was really loyal and virtuous. <br /> <br /> So if a part of the soul of the founder's became Shalim, or something, that's fine by me. That body and mind were a fetch mockery","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-16T00:00:39-07:00","id":1542231,"title":"","content":"To be fair I don't think that even the original poster believed what he posted as he comes across as a spammer going by his previous quotes a couple of months ago where he said a fair amount of absurd things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-17T04:30:51-07:00","id":1542304,"title":"","content":"Gratiano's embrace hints at the &quot;diablerie&quot; of Lasombra itself. From Clanbook: Lasombra Revised PG 22:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The details of Gratiano's escape are mundane<br /> enough, involving a body altered through blood magic<br /> to resemble him and left in his place </div> </div> </div>It makes quite a bit of sense that Lasombra would fake its death through a body double since it had that ability already. With the way high level Obtenabration and Abyss Mysticism is shown as written, going to the Abyss and existing as a Shadow being would be easy for it, but on the other hand, the things that exist there, are magnitudes older than something as mundane as an Antedeluvian vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26219-aydoo","name":"Aydoo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-17T09:04:18-07:00","id":1542316,"title":"","content":"He would be a lower level being in the Aybss, but maybe it was a price he was willing to pay for bypassing the curse of Caine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-17T15:37:51-07:00","id":1542338,"title":"","content":"Considering the Abyss according to DtF is the resting place of the Fallen, definitely. They're basically all Incarna level or higher beings. Lasombra was in for a rude awakening hahaha.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26219-aydoo","name":"Aydoo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-18T17:30:42-07:00","id":1542406,"title":"","content":"I can see that for a lot of the 3rd generation that they learn that as powerful as they are in the world of darkness, there is other older powers out there that are stronger and more cunning and dangerous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-20T19:52:55-07:00","id":1542473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1541954-lasombra-antediluvian?p=1542224#post1542224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Unless I misunderstood the original poster, that's pretty much how this thread was started. Even if others did not agree with it.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, you're right, I meant no one arguing that he plainly died said it was due to Diablerie.<br /> <br /> The OP does say he got diablerized, but also that he survived it just fine.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aydoo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1541954-lasombra-antediluvian?p=1542338#post1542338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering the Abyss according to DtF is the resting place of the Fallen, definitely. They're basically all Incarna level or higher beings. Lasombra was in for a rude awakening hahaha.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's no indication in the books that the &quot;Abyss&quot; from DtF and the &quot;Abyss&quot; from VtM are the same place.<br /> <br /> Or, by the way, the &quot;Abyss&quot; from WtA and the &quot;Abyss&quot; from WtO. Those are four places which may or may not be related, but work in very different ways in practice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-21T01:15:51-07:00","id":1542476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1541954-lasombra-antediluvian?p=1542473#post1542473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's no indication in the books that the &quot;Abyss&quot; from DtF and the &quot;Abyss&quot; from VtM are the same place.<br /> <br /> Or, by the way, the &quot;Abyss&quot; from WtA and the &quot;Abyss&quot; from WtO. Those are four places which may or may not be related, but work in very different ways in practice.</div> </div> </div> </div>From what I know, it goes like this.<br /> <br /> WTA Abyss: Most likely a reflection of the actual Abyss in the middle Umbra since it does hate all light and life like the actual Abyss/Void. Its bottom just leads to the Shadow Lands aka the Dark Umbra aka the Lower Umbra <br /> <br /> WTA Oblivion: The Nothingness at the bottom of the Shadowlands. Most likely the Void mentioned in DTF. Hates all of existence.<br /> <br /> DTF Abyss: While it does sound similar to others, it is most likely a pocket inside the actual Abyss or slightly above it like the Shadowlands since Fallen Angels are all alone in there. What other splats mention with the Abyss is usually called the Void here. Hates all life, light and existence.<br /> <br /> MTA Abyss: The thing Nephandi worships in one form or the other. DTF Void. Hates all light, life and existence.<br /> <br /> VTM Abyss: The Oblivion in the Underworld and the DTF The Void. Hates all light, life and existence.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27335-technoma","name":"Technoma","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-21T11:10:54-07:00","id":1542486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Technoma</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1541954-lasombra-antediluvian?p=1542476#post1542476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From what I know, it goes like this.<br /> <br /> WTA Abyss: Most likely a reflection of the actual Abyss in the middle Umbra since it does hate all light and life like the actual Abyss/Void. Its bottom just leads to the Shadow Lands aka the Dark Umbra aka the Lower Umbra<br /> <br /> WTA Oblivion: The Nothingness at the bottom of the Shadowlands. Most likely the Void mentioned in DTF. Hates all of existence.<br /> <br /> DTF Abyss: While it does sound similar to others, it is most likely a pocket inside the actual Abyss or slightly above it like the Shadowlands since Fallen Angels are all alone in there. What other splats mention with the Abyss is usually called the Void here. Hates all life, light and existence.<br /> <br /> MTA Abyss: The thing Nephandi worships in one form or the other. DTF Void. Hates all light, life and existence.<br /> <br /> VTM Abyss: The Oblivion in the Underworld and the DTF The Void. Hates all light, life and existence.</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s a good interpretation, but still an interpretation, that\u2019s my point.<br /> <br /> What we do have is this:<br /> <br /> WtA Abyss: it\u2019s a Realm in the Middle Umbra, called The Chasm by Mages. It actually looks like a rocky plateau full of caves and leading to a cliff, an actual, physical abyss. It has winds and is quite inhabited by a lot of things. It numbs the senses little by little, and can cause Harano.<br /> <br /> WtO Abyss/Oblivion: it\u2019s a place in the center/bottom of the Labyrinth. Since nothing that goes into it comes back, anything about it is speculation or legend. Neverborn and the Grandmother seem to come from this place, but they may just reside near it or whatever.<br /> <br /> VtM Abyss: it\u2019s a realm of complete sensory deprivation. Due to this, almost nothing can be said about it, except it doesn\u2019t actually trap people, it is just obviously hard to navigate. It is inhabited by beings seemingly made of shadow that can be summoned by some Abyss Mysticism rituals, but whether the rituals create them or just summon them, or if it has some effect on the forms they take, that\u2019s all in the air, as is any relationship between them and any other inhabitant of any other realm.<br /> <br /> MtA Void: it\u2019s actually on the outer reaches of the Umbra, so it\u2019s reached by going up instead of down, but it may have some link to the realms within the Earth. Nothing about it, even if it is just one place or actually several unrelated realms, is certain.<br /> <br /> DtF Abyss: it\u2019s a non-physical realm in the absolute sense, its inhabitants allegedly existing only as pure thought. It only contains demons, and as far as we know can\u2019t contain anything else. It has enough of a connection to other realms as to make it possible for some sort of sensory info to be perceived at intervals, but the details are muddled. It seems to be sensitive to Maelstroms at least, and to the Avatar Storm.<br /> <br /> As we can see, there\u2019s a lot of distinctions between those \u201cAbysses\u201d. Their common point is that more than unknown, something about them always remains unknowable. Either you won\u2019t come back from certain points, or you\u2019re sensory deprived and can\u2019t say for certain what\u2019s going on.<br /> <br /> But that\u2019s it. They could very well be completely unrelated and still work as they do just fine, or they can be distinct parts or distinct perspectives over the same phenomenon and work just fine all the same. What\u2019s important is that they fill different roles in their respective splats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-24T06:11:08-07:00","id":1542546,"title":"","content":"I'll just throw in that I also dislike the idea of beings who can't be defeated or killed. I'm more interested in the Dark Ages setting than the Modern Nights but I if would run a Modern Nights game then, yes, [Lasombra] and [Tzimisce] would be dead and killed by the Sabbat. Its entirely possible that these Ancients did have some kind of scheme to allow themselves to transcend by allowing themselves to be diablorized in the belief that they were so cunnig, powerful and erudite in all matters of relevance that they could pull this off.<br /> <br /> But it turned out they were not and could not.<br /> <br /> I also think that it would add to the Sabbat if they do have, even if in centuries past, some solid success in their war with the Antediluvians as opposed to be a bunch of hacks from start to finish.<br /> <br /> I do however realize that this goes against the accepted lore of the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-24T12:20:09-07:00","id":1542573,"title":"","content":"My quick thoughts on the matter.<br /> <br /> I'm going towards the idea that Lasombra itself is a shattered essence whom attempt to transcend failed and what we have left is fragments floating the void.<br /> <br /> 2. Tzismce is still around and can manifest himself through it's clan though it's easier with his direct childer or eldest grandchilder and it gets harder and harder to do it as blood potency thins down the generations.<br /> <br /> 3. Set is in Duat and is largely powerless on our plane, but can influence his clan into directions he wants.<br /> <br /> 4. Augustus Giovanni is gone due to the creation of the Hecate and there is nothing left of him at all.<br /> <br /> 5. Malkav became the Cobweb/Madness Network<br /> <br /> 6. Gangrel is part of the Earth and will exert her will from time to time.<br /> <br /> 7. Ravnos is still gone from the events of the Week Of Nightmares.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-26T10:12:17-07:00","id":1542692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1541954-lasombra-antediluvian?p=1542486#post1542486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It\u2019s a good interpretation, but still an interpretation, that\u2019s my point.<br /> <br /> What we do have is this:<br /> <br /> WtA Abyss: it\u2019s a Realm in the Middle Umbra, called The Chasm by Mages. It actually looks like a rocky plateau full of caves and leading to a cliff, an actual, physical abyss. It has winds and is quite inhabited by a lot of things. It numbs the senses little by little, and can cause Harano.<br /> <br /> WtO Abyss/Oblivion: it\u2019s a place in the center/bottom of the Labyrinth. Since nothing that goes into it comes back, anything about it is speculation or legend. Neverborn and the Grandmother seem to come from this place, but they may just reside near it or whatever.<br /> <br /> VtM Abyss: it\u2019s a realm of complete sensory deprivation. Due to this, almost nothing can be said about it, except it doesn\u2019t actually trap people, it is just obviously hard to navigate. It is inhabited by beings seemingly made of shadow that can be summoned by some Abyss Mysticism rituals, but whether the rituals create them or just summon them, or if it has some effect on the forms they take, that\u2019s all in the air, as is any relationship between them and any other inhabitant of any other realm.<br /> <br /> MtA Void: it\u2019s actually on the outer reaches of the Umbra, so it\u2019s reached by going up instead of down, but it may have some link to the realms within the Earth. Nothing about it, even if it is just one place or actually several unrelated realms, is certain.<br /> <br /> DtF Abyss: it\u2019s a non-physical realm in the absolute sense, its inhabitants allegedly existing only as pure thought. It only contains demons, and as far as we know can\u2019t contain anything else. It has enough of a connection to other realms as to make it possible for some sort of sensory info to be perceived at intervals, but the details are muddled. It seems to be sensitive to Maelstroms at least, and to the Avatar Storm.<br /> <br /> As we can see, there\u2019s a lot of distinctions between those \u201cAbysses\u201d. Their common point is that more than unknown, something about them always remains unknowable. Either you won\u2019t come back from certain points, or you\u2019re sensory deprived and can\u2019t say for certain what\u2019s going on.<br /> <br /> But that\u2019s it. They could very well be completely unrelated and still work as they do just fine, or they can be distinct parts or distinct perspectives over the same phenomenon and work just fine all the same. What\u2019s important is that they fill different roles in their respective splats.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> AHEM. We'll start with every splat not VtM, because they have the most fleshed out lore as well as the most connections. Lots of metaphysics here and I'll list specific books and pages for your own reading if you wish. We have a lot to cover...<br /> <br /> The Chasm of the Abyss, (also known as Umbral Realm of the Abyss, and the Maw of the Abyss,) exists both in WtA and MtA, within the Middle Umbra. A mage character of the supplement the <i>MtA: Book of Worlds </i>(pg 56-59) visits and describes it nearly exactly the same as it is described in both <i>WtA Umbra The Velvet Shadow </i>(pg 26-30) and <i>WtA Umbra</i> (pg 35-40.)I'm going to refer to it here as just the Chasm for simplicity sake.<br /> <br /> These books posit that the Chasm is a passage into/extension of the Umbral Realm of Malfeas (which is sometimes known as the Qlippoth Shard Realm of Entropy [<i>MtA Book of Madness</i> pg33]) which is tangentially connected to the WtO realm of the Labyrinth. These are all the path Entropy takes through the Umbra with, the Middle Umbra (Chasm), the Dark Umbra (Labyrinth, Abyss, Oblivion,) and the Deep Umbra (Malfeas.)<br /> <br /> <i>DtF Houses of the Fallen</i> pg 177-179 further explains that the Alabaster Legion of the host, built a fortress called Kasdeja and it was subsequently destroyed by Michael's host, so the Slayer Charon (DtF angel not WtO wraith) worked to carve out a realm called Haven from the nothingness below the world, which would later become known as the Underworld/Dark Umbra. Here he wanted to protect the souls of humans, and allow them to play with memory, till they could be shepherded instead of consigned to nothingness. Underneath the prime city which became known as Stygia, he carved out a fortress which would later be known as the Labyrinth. The Labyrinth helped separate Haven from the absolutely nothingness that the universe was carved out of.<br /> <br /> This nothingness is known in the splats as Oblivion, and has a consciousness which is both associated with the Wyrm (WtA,) Ialdabaoth (MtA,) and the Grand Maw(WtO)/Grandmother(Orpheus.) Entropy/Oblivion is suggested to be the opposite of Prime, making Grand Maw the opposite or dark reflection of God as they are thought to be avatars of their respective energies. This ties into the whole Yin/Yang aspect that all the splats follow. Vampire and the Beast, Wraiths and their Shadows, Mages and their Avatars, and Garou and their Gnosis/Rage are some examples of this.<br /> <br /> In <i>MtA: Book of Worlds</i> (pg 72-77) a character goes and meets with the Guildmaster of the Artificers, the Wraith Lord Ember, and enters the Labyrinth below Stygia for a time and talks about it from the standpoint of the Euthanatoi philosophies.<br /> <br /> Below the Labyrinth are two types of &quot;beings&quot; that exist as WtO explains the Once Born, which are just grossly powerful Spectres infused with powers of Entropy leaking from the nothingness of Oblivion, and the ever more powerful Neverborne, slumbering creatures that never had physical lives in the world.<br /> <br /> This is said in <i>DtF: Houses of the Fallen pg 179 </i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The second the doors of Hell sealed, the Slayers suddenly became aware of God's final punishment upon them. The walls around them were shaped from the substance of Haven itself, yet twisted and altered in such a way that they couldn't pass through it. That meant that the ruins of Haven, and all the souls within, lay just outside the Abyss, well within the reach of the Slayers' senses. </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> In the <i>core book</i> of DtF on pg 65, the narrative suggests that the Neverborne <b>are</b> the Fallen, and that the prison of the Abyss was located under Haven.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Maelstrom</b><br /> There were times when it seemed as though the walls of our prison might fall. Five times since our imprisonment a storm of terrible power raged across the spirit realm and battered against the seals of the Abyss. The most strident among us declared each time that the time of our release was at hand, that Creation was at an end, and that soon all our suffering would cease. Each time, they were wrong. We bathed in the hatred, fear and pain of the dead for a short time as they suffered in the throes of the Maelstrom. Afterwards we raged at the calm that settled in its wake, furious that nothing had changed. The gates of the Abyss remained as strong as ever, our freedom nothing more than a fading dream in a hate-filled mind.<br /> <br /> And then, in an instant, everything changed. We felt the surge in pain that marked another upheaval, sharp and fiery, filling us with pain and ecstasy. We flocked to the barrier between Hell and the realm of the dead, eager to increase the suffering of those souls we could reach and share in the pleasure we would reap. </div> </div> </div>Further on in the next section describes the route a Fallen took, through the Shadowlands, through the Maelstrom, to the Skinlands.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Exodus</b><br /> I hurled myself into the storm, heedless of its fury. All around me flew the ruined souls of those we tormented, and I tore through them, screaming my joy and my hate at the pathetic spirits that sought to bar my way. I rose through the storm, parting it before me, reaching upward from the Abyss to the world of the living. The dead clawed at me, the storm tried to grasp me, but neither could succeed for I was a demon, and I was free. </div> </div> </div>Even <i>MtA: Infinite Tapestry</i> suggests this as well with pg 26<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Strange beings -- spirits of things never born or dead since the inception of time and being -- skulk in even the Skinlands now, made brave by the greatly diminished numbers of souls that remain here. </div> </div> </div>The Umbral realms of the dead are layered in reverse from the physical world down towards Oblivion. The Dark Penumbra is the Shadowlands, then there is the Tempest below that. Further down are the Dark Kingdoms like Stygia and then the Labyrinth. Finally you have the Abyss and then Oblivion. When being are filled with more of the energy of entropy, they sink down until they reach Oblivion.<br /> <br /> This post is getting long enough as it is, I'll make another in regards to VtM specifically soon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26219,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26219-aydoo","user":"Aydoo","date":". 09-26-2024, 09:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26219-aydoo","name":"Aydoo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-26T12:02:16-07:00","id":1542706,"title":"","content":"The Abyss. Part two. Where VtM comes in.<br /> <br /> Mainly the practitioners of Abyss manipulation come the kindred line of the being known as Lasombra. The art is known as Obtenebration, and the further study of it codified into blood magic paths known as Abyss Mysticism. In the current 5th edition this power has been merged with the Necromancy abilities of the Revised and V20 eras into the discipline now known as <b><i>Oblivion</i></b>. This makes sense to be honest since both abilities are dealing with energies of Entropy and the Dark Umbra.<br /> <br /> In <i>VtDA: Player's Guide to the High Clans</i> pg 33,we get a story about how Lasombra, though it had rudimentry power of shadows, became obsessed with a more metaphysical Darkness and the Abyss during the time of the Flood that wiped away the First City Enoch.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Shadowed One was reborn into darkness through blood and pain. His mortal life, like his mortal name, is of no consequence. Sufficient to say that it was unremarkable in nearly every way. It is his immortal existence that concerns us, when he rose as a grandchilde of the Dark Father, one of the first of the third generation of the childer of Caine. He arose in<br /> the First City, ruled by the Dark Father and those of the second generation.<br /> <br /> From the very beginning, the Shadowed One remained close to the darkness that was his by right of blood. Shadows clung to him and the night was his home. Great cats stalked at his feet as he hunted and feasted, and slaves and servants feared and worshiped him. So it was for many nights, until the coming of the Great Flood that washed away the First City, showing the Shadowed One a greater darkness than even the starless night, the depths of the endless sea.<br /> <br /> How long he wandered its depths, none can say, existing wrapped in the arms of darkness, like being submerged in ink, beyond the reach of the sun. He existed and he hunted, the Shadowed One of the Deeps, in darkness and silence profound, the most feared predator of the seas, until the time when the floodwaters receded and the childer of Caine embraced the dry land once more. </div> </div> </div>This timeline of Caine's transformation into a vampire, then founding of Enoch to the Flood, coincides with the timeline of the Age of Wrath. The Age of Wrath is the thousand year war that lead to the fall and imprisonment of Lucifer's host in DtF. The Fallen first rebelled as an act of love for humans, and wanting to raise them up with knowledge but were barred from doing so. The war begins as non lethal duels, but turns when Caine murder's Abel, introducing a new concept into the universe. The Fallen help the humans build an empire known as Civilization of Ashes\u200b, and until it is all destroyed in an event called the Shattering. During the Shattering the Abyss itself is created and the majority of the Fallen are imprisoned.<br /> <br /> In <i>VtDA: Player's Guide to the High Clans</i> Pg158, and Pg 175-176 we have these descriptions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Staying in the Abyss for too long is not a good idea. Demonic creatures lurk in the Abyss and might decide to attack the character. In addition, the Abyss itself has an insidious influence upon those who stay there, and anyone spending too long in it might find himself becoming more and more obsessed with suffering and darkness.\u200b </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Abyss Mysticism</b><br /> <br /> As pragmatic as they are ruthless, most Lasombra regard Obtenebration as a tool. It is an important tool and a gift from their founder, but ultimately just one power among many. Only the most eccentric and arcane savants among the clan understand the true significance of their dark art. Obtenebration is more than mere shadow-play. It is a window to the Abyss itself, that great and terrible unknown that lies at the center of all things. The Abyss gnaws at the heart of the underworld and the doubt in every question never answered. It is present in the absence of light and lurks<br /> in every shadow. Ghosts rightly fear its hunger, but they do not understand it. Demons call it Hell, and they only begin to comprehend. No Lasombra knows where it comes from or its purpose or even the purpose of its strange denizens, but the clan\u2019s mystics know the Abyss is the ultimate source of their power. So the mystics vainly pry into the dark places in search of secrets and answers and perhaps more questions. For these driven souls, conventional Obtenebration is only the beginning. With rituals they unlock the hidden powers of shadow and summon the unnamed primordial horrors that lie beyond.\u200b </div> </div> </div>I'll be honest there is scant information about the Lasombra, Obtenebration, and Abyss Mysticism. Most books want to talk about the events of the Anarch Revolt, and the Sabbat/Antitribu split. The books that talk about the nature of Obtenebration are mostly in the Dark Ages version of the setting, and then the V20 era, which divorces itself from the World of Darkness as a cohesive whole.<br /> <br /> With the above you can see the intent of the authors, that was later built upon in revised editions of Mage the Ascension and the release of Demon the Fallen. Ultimately in your own game you get to decide what the Abyss actually is but if you read across all the splats, there is to me at least, a clear connection between these places and concepts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26219-aydoo","name":"Aydoo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-26T18:49:26-07:00","id":1542733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aydoo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1541954-lasombra-antediluvian?p=1542706#post1542706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With the above you can see the intent of the authors, that was later built upon in revised editions of Mage the Ascension and the release of Demon the Fallen. Ultimately in your own game you get to decide what the Abyss actually is but if you read across all the splats, there is to me at least, a clear connection between these places and concepts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe, but that was not the point. Most of this information is unreliable, and the definitions are vague, not strict. There are also contradictions galore, like the existence of things in the Abyss from Obtenebration that shouldn\u2019t exist in Hell according to DtF.<br /> <br /> Whichever intention the authors had, or didn\u2019t have, because they\u2019re not the same authors across lines and things change a lot through time, they kept those intentions as evasive suggestions by design.<br /> <br /> I explained the hard facts about those \u201cAbysses\u201d, and in that it is relevant that we never had any example of a user of Abyss Mysticism interacting with Demons in the Abyss, or Demons in Hell interacting with the strange beings Abyss Mystics can summon or encounter.<br /> <br /> Also, the distinction by splat is just didactic, nothing more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-26T20:08:35-07:00","id":1542746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1541954-lasombra-antediluvian?p=1542733#post1542733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe, but that was not the point. Most of this information is unreliable, and the definitions are vague, not strict. There are also contradictions galore, like the existence of things in the Abyss from Obtenebration that shouldn\u2019t exist in Hell according to DtF.<br /> <br /> Whichever intention the authors had, or didn\u2019t have, because they\u2019re not the same authors across lines and things change a lot through time, they kept those intentions as evasive suggestions by design.<br /> <br /> I explained the hard facts about those \u201cAbysses\u201d, and in that it is relevant that we never had any example of a user of Abyss Mysticism interacting with Demons in the Abyss, or Demons in Hell interacting with the strange beings Abyss Mystics can summon or encounter.<br /> <br /> Also, the distinction by splat is just didactic, nothing more.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I tend to think that the Abyss that Lasombra tap into is Oblivion in Wraith - specifically the creatures that it calls on and that exist within it are the bizarre ur-monstrosities that predate the creation universe and which can occasionally crawl out (of which Grandmother is the most well known). Oblivion itself is the last bit of primal darkness that existed before God said, &quot;Let there be light.&quot; The Prison that the Fallen were tapped in may have been coterminous to that location, but it's not the same place. As you point out, what we've seen of the Lasombra's Abyss and what we've seen of the prison in which the Fallen were kept, these are two very different places with different rules and conceptual space.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-27T05:51:51-07:00","id":1542761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1541954-lasombra-antediluvian?p=1542733#post1542733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe, but that was not the point. Most of this information is unreliable, and the definitions are vague, not strict. There are also contradictions galore, like the existence of things in the Abyss from Obtenebration that shouldn\u2019t exist in Hell according to DtF.<br /> <br /> Whichever intention the authors had, or didn\u2019t have, because they\u2019re not the same authors across lines and things change a lot through time, they kept those intentions as evasive suggestions by design.<br /> <br /> I explained the hard facts about those \u201cAbysses\u201d, and in that it is relevant that we never had any example of a user of Abyss Mysticism interacting with Demons in the Abyss, or Demons in Hell interacting with the strange beings Abyss Mystics can summon or encounter.<br /> <br /> Also, the distinction by splat is just didactic, nothing more.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> &quot;Just trust me bro.&quot; does not facts make. I too could hand wave all your &quot;facts&quot; away with the same logic you are using. In the same token you are also using the same &quot;unreliable information, vague non strict definitions, and contradictions.&quot; This isn't conducive to a discussion and is just dismissive. You didn't bother reading the posts since there is in fact evidence of Lasombra interacting with such. Not every book is written through a mode of fiction, some are just written as game material, or do you take every book that has mechanics and lists things such as Merits and Flaws as &quot;unreliable information?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26219-aydoo","name":"Aydoo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-27T11:46:45-07:00","id":1542788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aydoo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1541954-lasombra-antediluvian?p=1542761#post1542761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> &quot;Just trust me bro.&quot; does not facts make. I too could hand wave all your &quot;facts&quot; away with the same logic you are using. In the same token you are also using the same &quot;unreliable information, vague non strict definitions, and contradictions.&quot; This isn't conducive to a discussion and is just dismissive. You didn't bother reading the posts since there is in fact evidence of Lasombra interacting with such. Not every book is written through a mode of fiction, some are just written as game material, or do you take every book that has mechanics and lists things such as Merits and Flaws as &quot;unreliable information?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>At this point I don't think you understood anything I said.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m not saying they\u2019re unrelated. I\u2019m saying their relationship is up to the ST.<br /> <br /> My \u201cfacts\u201d are strictly the confirmed rules on interactions with those realms.<br /> <br /> Your proposition is valid, but isn\u2019t strictly canon. I.e. if someone decides to not follow them, they\u2019re not contradicting the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-02T23:57:44-07:00","id":1543050,"title":"","content":"Isn't a given that we all take certain creative liberties with the metaplot anyway. We could have Lasombra failing in his attempt to transcend his curse to Brujah suffering from a split personality since the embrace and it being an answer why his or her personality is so unpredictable and not anything to do with amaranth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-03T15:39:32-07:00","id":1543069,"title":"","content":"Yes, but canonicity is important in some contexts. Not only is it important to some people that feel uncomfortable deviating from it, it forms the basis for communication within the community and with/between the authors (even when you depart from it, you start from it), and it is the basis for new developments.<br /> <br /> As an author of my own chronicles, I know myself that sometimes I\u2019ll have a clear idea of how something will relate to everything else, I\u2019ll even drop some hints, but I\u2019ll purposefuly avoid making it canon because I need some wiggle room, or making it canon closes too many options that I may want to have later.<br /> <br /> So however much the authors hint at something being a possible explanation, as long as they actively avoid making it canon, there is a reason for doing so, and assuming it as truth may not really improve anything. Unless it is the only possible explanation and one is needed, which isn\u2019t the case with the Abyss(es).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-03T19:26:55-07:00","id":1543077,"title":"","content":"Fair enough Monteparnas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-06T15:51:48-07:00","id":1543223,"title":"","content":"My notion is that Lasombra is in the Void learning new powers that he couldn't use when he still had a physical form and that he uses Gratino as a meat puppet when he needs things done but doesn't have the time to do it himself or his new form comes with new limitations that he didn't anticipate.<br /> <br /> As with Brujah I go with idea that he was mentally ill before the embrace and as time goes it goes worse and we see a split personality where he or she can be calm, cool and logical one night and extremely short tempered and ready to kill at a moment's notice. It doesn't really alter the metaplot much for those who really concern themselves with the lore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-07T14:25:57-07:00","id":1543285,"title":"","content":"Something that hasn't been mentioned yet (I think) is that some of the vitae of the Lasombra antediluvian is supposed to be contained with the body of the Hulul, the eldest member of the Assamite antitribu, an ersatz replacement for the Old Man of the Mountain. Every hundred years the Hulul is then ritually diablerized by another Assamite anti-tribu who then becomes the next Hulul for the next century until he gets diablerized.<br /> <br /> The Revised era Guide to the Sabbat suggests this is done as a sacrifice to Caine, though I believe this was not mentioned in earlier sourcebooks. The concept of the Hulul is quite strange and not adequately explained. Why would any vampire want to become the Hulul? Why are the assamite anti-tribu doing it at all? Yeah, such a rising and dying &quot;king&quot; has antecedents in mortal mythology, but why did it develop here?<br /> <br /> So Gratiano was not the only vampire to drink Lasombra's blood (supposedly). This may be why Gratiano does not seem to be the generation of Lasombra. I wonder if there was some sort of attempt by Gratiano, the Assamites, and any other flunkies who attacked to use something like the Ritual of the Bitter Rose. That ritual in some earlier format was supposedly created by ancient, mythic vampires (like the Wanderer) before the current version was invented in the late 19th century. We also know that the Ritual of the Bitter Rose sometimes produces odd results like the victim's vitae having no potency (and thus giving no benefit to the diablerists), the diablerists gaining derangements, aggravated damage, explode in flame, or that vitae can be stored for later use. Perhaps the idea was that multiple vampires could increase their generation.<br /> <br /> Then there is the additional oddity that in Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand we learn that the original Assamite antitribu (the Assamites who helped the Anarchs) were actually rogue Assamites who defected from the Old Man of the Mountain to serve the True Hand centuries before the Anarch Revolt. The True Hand sent agents to the Anarchs to help them destroy the elders of the clans, as they consider the elders to be enemies of the antediluvians. This is probably the reason why the organization of the Assamite anti-tribu is so different from the rest of the Sabbat clans - it's to allow the clan's elders to keep their secret allegiance to the True Black Hand unknown and recruit newer Assamite anti-tribu into the TBH once they have proved their worth/loyalty.<br /> <br /> If we assume the lore of DSBH to be true, than Gratiano attacked Lasombra with Assamites who were loyal to the True Black Hand and thus highly unlikely to actually want to kill Lasombra. They want to lead the Anarchs against disobedient elders like Gratiano, not against the antediluvians like Lasombra. This leaves open some possibilities. First, the Assamites who accompanied Gratiano likely sabotaged the diablerie attempt so that it would fail. Second, they either used Gratiano as a dupe or there is an even darker secret out there. <br /> <br /> Perhaps Gratiano wasn't really an Anarch, but a member of the True Black Hand who never intended to diablerize Lasombra, but to fulfill the sect's purpose (and perhaps his sire's) and everything we know about Gratiano in Children of the Inquisition is just the cover story he's been putting out all this time. He didn't take over leadership of the Sabbat Lasombra and remains content as a &quot;mere&quot; archbishop of the sect because he doesn't actually believe in the sect, and is acting as a deep cover agent for the True Black Hand waiting until the right moment to strike. There are obviously <i>lots</i> of issues with this theory and I don't think it's necessarily true or likely, but I also don't think it can be dismissed outright simply because there are a lot of strange things about this event.<br /> <br /> However, going back to the Hulul, assuming the Hulul do trace their &quot;line&quot; to members of the True Black Hand, what purpose is the entire diablerie ritual every hundred years? Is there actually any vitae of Lasombra within the Hulul at all? If there is, are they preserving it on purpose? Is this somehow keeping Lasombra in existence? Are the Hulul actually being destroyed? Or is the entire ritual and concept of the Hulul an excuse to extract their deep cover agents within the False Hand so they can safely go back to their real sect? Or is it for some other reason?<br /> <br /> I know that much lore of the DSBH was abandoned in Revised and later, and thus using it is a non-starter for many players. If so, the story of the Hulul will play out much differently. However, I have to think that some of what I laid out above was in fact the plan of Vampire's original developer, Andrew Greenberg, the writer of the original Sabbat books Steven Brown, and the writer of Children of the Inquisition, Dan Greenberg (Andrew's brother).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-07T15:26:51-07:00","id":1543289,"title":"","content":"That's something I wouldn't consider, but as you said Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand wasn't well received by the fans and has been ignored by later supplements.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-07T23:35:15-07:00","id":1543326,"title":"","content":"Even if you ignore the lore of DSBH, one should still need to address the Hulul and its possession of the vitae of Lasombra as that has held even in editions where DSBH was disparaged.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-08T00:02:15-07:00","id":1543330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1541954-lasombra-antediluvian?p=1543285#post1543285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, going back to the Hulul, assuming the Hulul do trace their &quot;line&quot; to members of the True Black Hand, what purpose is the entire diablerie ritual every hundred years? Is there actually any vitae of Lasombra within the Hulul at all? If there is, are they preserving it on purpose? Is this somehow keeping Lasombra in existence? Are the Hulul actually being destroyed? Or is the entire ritual and concept of the Hulul an excuse to extract their deep cover agents within the False Hand so they can safely go back to their real sect? Or is it for some other reason?</div> </div> </div> </div>You know we &quot;seen&quot; something like this before<br /> Or something <i>very</i> similar<br /> After the fall of the Second City, Malkav is believed to have traveled towards the city of Petra. It is along this journey that some think the Eldest Malkavian was attacked and torn asunder. Yet even if his body was destroyed, it is believed that his spirit survived inside of his childer, who gathered at the site of his death and drank his spilled blood, taking Malkav's essence into them and sheltering it from the sun's rays.<br /> A vampire not fully destroyed untill his Heart's blood is destroyed and if anyone the Children of Haqim know <i>eveything</i> about the Heart&quot;s blood - their studies of vitae have isolated the part within a vampire's blood that contains the soul. They call it &quot;heart's blood&quot; and it manifests as a thick, blackish liquid that quickly grows dry when it leaves the body. Via applications of Quietus they are able to manipulate the heart's blood to allow them to diablerize a victim later. Furthermore, studies in Quietus have found a way to force the last drop of vitae within a vampire's body to calcify the heart into a semi-translucent grayish-white flask known as a &quot;<i>Debitum</i>&quot;. The Debitum enshrouds the spiritual essence (the &quot;heart's-blood&quot;) of the victim \u2013 which, if examined in detail, can be seen encased within, swimming in despair. Heart\u2019s-blood preserved in this way endures indefinitely. (Dark Ages: Vampire Rulebook, p. 209, Vampire Twentieth Anniversary Edition: The Dark Ages, p. 244)<br /> Following this logic with a side tangent, here is that little V5 thing, called:<br /> &quot;<b>Blood of Zapathasura</b>&quot; - Thick, <b>sentient</b> ropes of his vitae stained the ground in Bangladesh where he fell. The noonday sun <b>did not destroy it all</b>. You own a small vial containing the Blood of the Ravnos Antediluvian. What you do with this vitae is up to you, and what it does to anyone who imbibes it is up to the Storyteller.<br /> Funny to think, Zapathasura became Venom-like Anyhow, Malkav survived destruction and became the Madness Network and are inside his Clan... Maybe Zappy pulled a Malkav<br /> And the Lasombra antedulivan did the same mayhaps?<br /> <br /> Now Malkav's case is very similar whats happened with Lasombra - a Group &quot;diablerie&quot; without anyone becoming 3rd gen - just like in the case of the Lasombra Antediluvian's attackers, Gratiano and co. <br /> <br /> Like the True Vessel in Cappadocius and Augustus' case... it could be the Lasombra Antediluvian's &quot;backup plan&quot; or linchpin to the world...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 10-08-2024, 04:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-08T07:37:55-07:00","id":1543338,"title":"","content":"All I can say is wow Shadeprowler.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-08T11:16:32-07:00","id":1543352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1541954-lasombra-antediluvian?p=1543330#post1543330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know we &quot;seen&quot; something like this before...<br /> <br /> Like the True Vessel in Cappadocius and Augustus' case... it could be the Lasombra Antediluvian's &quot;backup plan&quot; or linchpin to the world...</div> </div> </div> </div>Very interesting. That Dark Ages text obviously comes way after the original mention of the Hulul, but it does provide a really interesting explanation that is very compelling. The Assamite diablerists who attacked Lasombra with Gratiano could be doing this if DSBH style they wanted to preserve him, or if we ignore DSBH then they may have their own secret reason why they haven't finished the diablerie yet.<br /> <br /> It still doesn't explain why the Hulul is ritually destroyed every century or why the elders of the Assamite anti-tribu agree to be diablerized. If we assume this tradition always existed, then we've six Hulus diablerized since the attack on Lasombra (1505, 1605, 1705, 1805, 1905 and 2005 assuming it happened on the first century anniversary of the diablerie). Vampires sacrificing themselves are very rare, so a whole line of them doing so is even more unusual. Does it have to do with their understanding of the Path of Caine? Is it needed to preserve the heart's blood? Is it part of some secret ritual that provides some benefit? What about the position of the Hulul makes it worth to only exist for only a hundred years afterwards?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-08T12:02:02-07:00","id":1543353,"title":"","content":"Sounds like a great story idea for my Malkavian down the road.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-08T12:10:56-07:00","id":1543355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1541954-lasombra-antediluvian?p=1543352#post1543352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It still doesn't explain why the Hulul is ritually destroyed every century or why the elders of the Assamite anti-tribu agree to be diablerized.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>My headcanon is - and nothing really supports it, just sounds strangely &quot;logical&quot; is the wayward &quot;Assamites&quot; was influenced by an extent the Clan on and off allies, the Salubri<br /> In 1133 Saulot was diablerized by Tremere and following that, following their Father's footsteps many - almost all, except the likes of Nehum ben Enosh - including the venerable Mokur more often than not voluntarily offerred themselves to be diablerized...<br /> The Children of Haqim had a love/hate relationship with the Salubri; Haqim never really trusted Saulot (especially after he basically forced on to him the position of &quot;Lawkeeper&quot;) and the whole Baali wars were a mess<br /> Still the Warriors fought side by side with the Children of Haqim and later the Ashirra offered protection to the Al-Amin &quot;The Virtuous Ones&quot; under the condition - thanks to an accord between the Old Man of the Mountain and Nahum ben Enosh - their numbers never surpass seven and the protection only extends to the Ashirra controlled terriotry<br /> However there is another group of Salubri, called the Seven - the public face of the clan - who hanged with elder Malkavians like their Antediluvian and somehow along the line developed the practice to attain Golconda then let their Childe diablerize them (igroning the fact Golconda suposedly make you immune to diableri) - probably thanks to the Malkavian's insanity they loved to hang with<br /> Now since the Antitribu as it was pointed out not really folloed the edicts of the main clan I think it is higly possible the two group degenerated together so to speak: the &quot;suicidal&quot; Seven were a &quot;Bad Influence&quot; on the Antitribu (who even maybe followed the Ashirra example and protected those Seven outside the Ashirra terriotry and the Main Clan's area of influence) and the Hulul adopted the practice and philopsophy of the Seven and the whole Amaranth in every century is a form of those Salubri's believes twised and adopted<br /> [Maybe paired with the last joke from the Antediluvian since no one actually who been there could recall what and how actually happened - they just remeber they done the deed (smells like a Dominate) - Lasombra coded i nto them: my &quot;killers&quot; will be killed voluntarily, like me!]<br /> <br /> To them, it is a secred duty they have to pass on and they know they will die<br /> But it is the sign of their &quot;Faith&quot;<br /> There is a similar instance in Etiopia.<br /> <b>T</b>he Ethiopian Orthodox Tewahedo Church claims to possess the Ark of the Covenant in Axum. The Ark is kept under guard in a treasury near the Church of Our Lady Mary of Zion. They supposedly protect the Ark of the Covenant since Menelik, the son of the Queen of Sheba and King Solomon &quot;borrowed it without asking&quot; around 3000 years ago<br /> Now the Ark have a... very unhealthy effect on its guardians,<br /> To be the custodian of the Ark is a great honor but it's also a death sentence<br /> The priests who guard the Ark have a very short lifespan. Once appointed a guardian they typically live no more than two or three years but before they die they develop cataracts and go blind<br /> Yet to them it is a great honor<br /> <br /> Similar could be the case with the Hulul\u200b<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-08T13:10:12-07:00","id":1543357,"title":"","content":"For greater clarity I meant that my Malkavian should try to learn about what possibly happened to Malkav in the past.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-08T16:44:35-07:00","id":1543371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1541954-lasombra-antediluvian?p=1543352#post1543352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It still doesn't explain why the Hulul is ritually destroyed every century or why the elders of the Assamite anti-tribu agree to be diablerized. If we assume this tradition always existed, then we've six Hulus diablerized since the attack on Lasombra (1505, 1605, 1705, 1805, 1905 and 2005 assuming it happened on the first century anniversary of the diablerie). Vampires sacrificing themselves are very rare, so a whole line of them doing so is even more unusual. Does it have to do with their understanding of the Path of Caine? Is it needed to preserve the heart's blood? Is it part of some secret ritual that provides some benefit? What about the position of the Hulul makes it worth to only exist for only a hundred years afterwards?</div> </div> </div> </div>What if those particular Assamite antitribu aren't members of the Tal'Mahe'Ra, and their aim is something like containment rather than service? Maybe the Lasombra antediluvian couldn't be truly destroyed by any measures the Anarchs were capable of, but it could be neutralized for a time by diablerie, with the ritual sacrifice turning the duty over to a fresh warden before the current Hulul could be overcome and supplanted from within?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-08T19:32:14-07:00","id":1543381,"title":"","content":"Hey that could be a great story idea and it would fit in with the lore Matt The Bruins Fan. We do know that very old and powerful Kindred can survive amaranth and can slowly influence at the very least to outright control there new form.<br /> <br /> We have seen that with Coventry being overwhelmed by the power of Mithras and Michael guiding Mariah for his own ends.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-09T16:02:06-07:00","id":1543458,"title":"","content":"It would be interesting to see some tidbits if how the 3rd generation kindred attempts to bypass the 